35:["$","footer",null,{"className":"site-footer","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"shell footer-grid","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"className":"brand footer-brand","href":"/","children":["$","img",null,{"className":"brand-logo brand-logo-dark","src":"/Logos/OW%20web%20desktop%20logos%20(200%20x%2040%20px)/OW%20White%20Logo%20desktop.png","alt":"One Window"}]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Expert guidance and technology for your study abroad journey."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Explore"}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/#destinations","children":"Study destinations"}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/countries","children":"Universities"}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/#consultation","children":"Course guidance"}],["$","$Lf",null,{"href":"/careers","children":"Careers"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Connect"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://onewindow.co/contact/","children":"Contact"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"mailto:info@onewindow.co","children":"Email us"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://onewindow.co/privacy-policy/","children":"Privacy policy"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"shell footer-bottom","children":"© One Window. All rights reserved."}]]}]
36:["$","p","Students can get support with university shortlisting, course selection, application documentation, visa guidance, interview preparation, and pre-departure planning.",{"children":"Students can get support with university shortlisting, course selection, application documentation, visa guidance, interview preparation, and pre-departure planning."}]
37:["$","p","The goal is to help students make smarter study abroad decisions, not just faster ones.",{"children":"The goal is to help students make smarter study abroad decisions, not just faster ones."}]
38:["$","p","One Window Overseas Education supports students from the initial counselling stage to the final stages of their study abroad journey. This may include profile evaluation, course and university shortlisting, application assistance, documentation guidance, visa filing support, mock interview preparation, and pre-departure guidance.",{"children":"One Window Overseas Education supports students from the initial counselling stage to the final stages of their study abroad journey. This may include profile evaluation, course and university shortlisting, application assistance, documentation guidance, visa filing support, mock interview preparation, and pre-departure guidance."}]
39:["$","p","The team also helps students understand country-specific requirements, financial planning, accommodation basics, and important next steps before travelling abroad.",{"children":"The team also helps students understand country-specific requirements, financial planning, accommodation basics, and important next steps before travelling abroad."}]
3a:["$","p","The duration of a study abroad programme depends on the country, course, and level of study. Most master’s programmes in Europe take 1 to 2 years to complete. Bachelor’s programmes usually take 3 to 4 years, depending on the country and academic structure.",{"children":"The duration of a study abroad programme depends on the country, course, and level of study. Most master’s programmes in Europe take 1 to 2 years to complete. Bachelor’s programmes usually take 3 to 4 years, depending on the country and academic structure."}]
3b:["$","p","MBA programmes may take 1 to 2 years, while diploma, foundation, language, and pathway programmes may have shorter durations.",{"children":"MBA programmes may take 1 to 2 years, while diploma, foundation, language, and pathway programmes may have shorter durations."}]
3c:["$","p","Students should always check the exact course duration before applying.",{"children":"Students should always check the exact course duration before applying."}]
3d:["$","p","Yes, many countries allow international students to work part-time while studying. The number of permitted working hours depends on the country and visa rules.",{"children":"Yes, many countries allow international students to work part-time while studying. The number of permitted working hours depends on the country and visa rules."}]
3e:["$","p","Part-time work can help students gain exposure, improve communication skills, understand local work culture, and manage some living expenses. However, students should not depend entirely on part-time income to fund their education.",{"children":"Part-time work can help students gain exposure, improve communication skills, understand local work culture, and manage some living expenses. However, students should not depend entirely on part-time income to fund their education."}]
3f:["$","p","Work rights, wage levels, and post-study work options vary from country to country, so students should check the official rules before applying.",{"children":"Work rights, wage levels, and post-study work options vary from country to country, so students should check the official rules before applying."}]
40:["$","p","Some European countries allow international students to bring a spouse or dependent family member, but the rules vary by country, course level, visa type, and financial capacity.",{"children":"Some European countries allow international students to bring a spouse or dependent family member, but the rules vary by country, course level, visa type, and financial capacity."}]
41:["$","p","Countries such as the UK, Finland, Denmark, and the Netherlands may have dependent or spouse visa options under specific conditions. Other countries may have different rules or restrictions.",{"children":"Countries such as the UK, Finland, Denmark, and the Netherlands may have dependent or spouse visa options under specific conditions. Other countries may have different rules or restrictions."}]
42:["$","p","Students planning to apply with a spouse should check financial requirements, accommodation proof, visa rules, dependent work rights, and timelines before applying.",{"children":"Students planning to apply with a spouse should check financial requirements, accommodation proof, visa rules, dependent work rights, and timelines before applying."}]
43:["$","p","The main benefits of studying in Europe include:",{"children":"The main benefits of studying in Europe include:"}]
44:["$","p","Globally recognised degrees",{"children":"Globally recognised degrees"}]
45:["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","What is VFS in the student visa process?",{"children":"What is VFS in the student visa process?"}],["$","li","How can a Europe education consultant help me?",{"children":"How can a Europe education consultant help me?"}],["$","li","Why choose One Window Overseas Education for Europe studies?",{"children":"Why choose One Window Overseas Education for Europe studies?"}],["$","li","How does One Window Overseas Education support students during the study abroad process?",{"children":"How does One Window Overseas Education support students during the study abroad process?"}],["$","li","How long do study abroad programmes usually take?",{"children":"How long do study abroad programmes usually take?"}],["$","li","Can Indian students work while studying abroad?",{"children":"Can Indian students work while studying abroad?"}],["$","li","Can I apply for a study visa with my spouse?",{"children":"Can I apply for a study visa with my spouse?"}],["$","li","What are the main benefits of studying in Europe?",{"children":"What are the main benefits of studying in Europe?"}]]}]
46:["$","p","Students can also book a counselling session to understand which European country fits their profile, budget, and career goals.",{"children":"Students can also book a counselling session to understand which European country fits their profile, budget, and career goals."}]
47:["$","p","One Window Overseas Education may support students with pre-departure and initial settlement guidance, depending on the destination and service plan. This can include guidance related to accommodation, travel preparation, airport arrival basics, local documentation, student essentials, and initial adjustment support.",{"children":"One Window Overseas Education may support students with pre-departure and initial settlement guidance, depending on the destination and service plan. This can include guidance related to accommodation, travel preparation, airport arrival basics, local documentation, student essentials, and initial adjustment support."}]
48:["$","p","The goal is to help students feel more prepared before and after they travel abroad.",{"children":"The goal is to help students feel more prepared before and after they travel abroad."}]
49:["$","p","Admission processing time depends on the university, country, course, intake, and application volume. In general, students may receive an admission decision within 15 to 90 days.",{"children":"Admission processing time depends on the university, country, course, intake, and application volume. In general, students may receive an admission decision within 15 to 90 days."}]
4a:["$","p","Some universities may respond faster, while competitive programmes or public universities may take longer. Students should apply early to avoid missing visa deadlines and scholarship opportunities.",{"children":"Some universities may respond faster, while competitive programmes or public universities may take longer. Students should apply early to avoid missing visa deadlines and scholarship opportunities."}]
4b:["$","p","A complete and well-prepared application can reduce delays.",{"children":"A complete and well-prepared application can reduce delays."}]
4c:["$","p","Yes, a study gap may be accepted for Europe student visa applications, depending on the country, university, course, and reason for the gap. Students should be able to explain the gap clearly with supporting documents.",{"children":"Yes, a study gap may be accepted for Europe student visa applications, depending on the country, university, course, and reason for the gap. Students should be able to explain the gap clearly with supporting documents."}]
4d:["$","p","Work experience, internships, exam preparation, family reasons, health reasons, or skill development may be acceptable if properly documented.",{"children":"Work experience, internships, exam preparation, family reasons, health reasons, or skill development may be acceptable if properly documented."}]
4e:["$","p","A study gap does not automatically lead to rejection, but students must show academic seriousness, financial readiness, and a clear reason for choosing the course and country.",{"children":"A study gap does not automatically lead to rejection, but students must show academic seriousness, financial readiness, and a clear reason for choosing the course and country."}]
4f:["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Why study a master’s programme in Europe?",{"children":"Why study a master’s programme in Europe?"}],["$","li","Why study management programmes in France?",{"children":"Why study management programmes in France?"}],["$","li","How can I contact One Window Overseas Education for Europe study guidance?",{"children":"How can I contact One Window Overseas Education for Europe study guidance?"}],["$","li","What support does One Window Overseas Education provide after students reach Europe?",{"children":"What support does One Window Overseas Education provide after students reach Europe?"}],["$","li","How long does it take to get admission to a European university?",{"children":"How long does it take to get admission to a European university?"}],["$","li","Is a study gap accepted for Europe student visa?",{"children":"Is a study gap accepted for Europe student visa?"}]]}]
